From fd28400c1c5b944469c52264394958a6bd70d2b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mdjavad2nd prf <md.javad01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:01:04 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] feat(playback): truthful streamType, videoType,
 watermarkFullName (v1.8.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three additive keys on the playback contract. No schema change; every existing
key is unchanged, so the shipped web PWA is unaffected.

1. streamType was hard-coded "hls" while the server serves MP4. A client
   trusting it would initialise an HLS player against a plain MP4. It is now
   derived from the lesson's own video_url via detect_video_type().

   The rule is deliberately conservative: ONLY a .m3u8 suffix means HLS,
   everything else is MP4. The admin can paste any URL into the video field —
   the plugin validates only https and the host allowlist, never the extension
   — and in proxy mode the URL has no extension at all. webm/mov therefore
   report mp4; Media3 uses the same data source for all of them, so the
   distinction has no behavioural consequence and a third type would widen the
   contract for nothing. A filter (mrdastbaaf_stream_video_type) covers the
   real-HLS future, and an unsupported value from it is rejected back to mp4
   rather than leaking through.

2. watermarkFullName. The client needed name + id + masked phone for the
   watermark, but the name only existed in GET /auth/me — which an anonymous
   free-preview playback never calls, so a guest got no name at all.
   build_watermark() now returns a name key, surfaced on both the ticket and
   the playback responses, with a fallback for an empty display_name so the
   watermark never renders a blank segment. Identity stays server-provided,
   never derived client-side.

3. qualities[].type — per-quality discriminator, since a client must not sniff
   the extension (proxy URLs have none).

Also: build_watermark() is now called once per playback response instead of
separately in each branch.

Tests: tests/php/test-video-type.php — 16 assertions covering the MP4 default,
the .m3u8 rule including case-insensitivity and signed query strings, the
extension-less proxy shape, malformed/empty URLs, a path segment literally
named m3u8, a .mp4 segment under an hls/ directory, and all three filter
outcomes. Suite totals 100 assertions across four files.

Docs: docs/PLUGIN_v1.8.0_VIDEO_TYPE_AND_WATERMARK_NAME.md
