@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# Plugin change — `videoType` and `watermarkFullName`
+
+**Version:** bridge `1.8.0` · **Schema:** unchanged (`1.7.0`)
+**Unblocks:** a single-source watermark and a reliable MP4↔HLS switch in the player.
+
+Two small additive changes to the playback contract. No schema change, no
+behaviour change for existing clients — every new key is optional and every
+existing key is unchanged.
+
+---
+
+## 1. `streamType` was lying
+
+`POST /lessons/{id}/playback-ticket` hard-coded `"streamType": "hls"` while the
+server serves **MP4**. A client that trusted that field would initialise an HLS
+player against a plain MP4 file.
+
+It is now derived from the lesson's own `video_url` via
+`MrDastbaaf_Courses_Controller::detect_video_type()`.
+
+### The detection rule
+
+**Only a `.m3u8` suffix means HLS. Everything else is MP4.**
+
+This is deliberately conservative. The admin can paste any URL into a lesson's
+video field — the plugin validates only `https://` and the host allowlist, never
+the extension — and in proxy mode the URL has no extension at all
+(`/lessons/{id}/stream?token=…`). An optimistic guess would be wrong exactly when
+it matters.
+
+`webm`, `mov` and friends therefore report `mp4`. Media3 uses the same
+`DefaultHttpDataSource` for all of them, so the distinction has no behavioural
+consequence, and adding a third type would widen the contract for nothing.
+
+A filter is provided for when real HLS (or DASH) lands, so no core code needs to
+change:
+
+```php
+add_filter('mrdastbaaf_stream_video_type', function ($type, $url, $lesson_id) {
+    return 'hls';
+}, 10, 3);
+```
+
+An unsupported value from the filter is rejected back to `mp4` rather than
+leaking through.
+
+---
+
+## 2. `watermarkFullName`
+
+The app needed **name + user id + masked phone** for the player watermark, but
+the full name only existed in `GET /auth/me` — which an anonymous free-preview
+playback never calls. The client was forced to merge two sources, and got no name
+at all for a guest.
+
+`build_watermark()` now returns a `name` key, surfaced as `watermarkFullName` on
+both the ticket and the playback responses.
+
+| Caller | `watermarkText` | `watermarkUserId` | `watermarkFullName` |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Signed in | `0912***4567 \| ID: 42` | `"42"` | the user's `display_name` |
+| Guest (free preview) | `مهمان \| مستر دستباف` | `"guest"` | `مهمان` |
+
+The name comes from the server, never derived client-side — the same rule that
+already applied to `text` and `user_id`. A user whose `display_name` is empty
+falls back to `هنرجو` so the watermark never renders a blank segment.
+
+---
+
+## Full response shapes
+
+### `POST /lessons/{id}/playback-ticket`
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "ticketId": "tkt_aB3xY9kLmN2pQ4rT",
+  "lessonId": "12",
+  "expiresInSeconds": 900,
+  "issuedAt": "2026-10-16T08:00:00+00:00",
+  "expiresAt": "2026-10-16T08:15:00+00:00",
+  "watermarkText": "0912***4567 | ID: 42",
+  "watermarkUserId": "42",
+  "watermarkFullName": "محمدجواد فلان",   // NEW
+  "streamType": "mp4"                     // was hard-coded "hls"
+}
+```
+
+### `POST /lessons/{id}/playback` — direct mode (default)
+
+```jsonc
+{
+  "videoUrl": "https://dll.mrdastbaaf.com/FA/lesson-01.mp4",
+  "videoType": "mp4",                     // NEW
+  "watermarkText": "0912***4567 | ID: 42",
+  "watermarkUserId": "42",
+  "watermarkFullName": "محمدجواد فلان",   // NEW
+  "expiresAt": "2026-10-16T08:15:00+00:00",
+  "qualities": [
+    { "label": "1080p", "url": "https://…/lesson-01-1080.mp4", "type": "mp4" }  // `type` NEW
+  ],
+  "proxyMode": false
+}
+```
+
+### `POST /lessons/{id}/playback` — proxy mode
+
+Same keys; `videoType` reflects the **source** type, because the proxy streams the
+source bytes through unchanged.
+
+---
+
+## Client guidance
+
+- **Do not sniff the extension.** Read `videoType`; fall back to `streamType` from
+  the ticket; only then guess. In proxy mode the URL has no extension, so sniffing
+  fails outright.
+- `watermarkFullName` is authoritative — do not substitute the locally cached
+  profile name, which may be stale or absent for a guest.
+
+## Tests
+
+`tests/php/test-video-type.php` — 16 assertions, no WordPress required (the two
+WordPress functions it needs are stubbed in the file, the same way the other
+tests stub `ABSPATH`):
+
+```bash
+./tests/php/run-all.sh
+```
+
+Covers the MP4 default, the `.m3u8` rule including case-insensitivity and signed
+query strings, the extension-less proxy shape, malformed and empty URLs, a path
+segment literally named `m3u8`, a `.mp4` segment under an `hls/` directory, and
+all three filter outcomes (promote to HLS, reject an unsupported type, reject
+null).
+
+## Staging checklist
+
+- [ ] `POST /lessons/{id}/playback-ticket` on an MP4 lesson returns `streamType: "mp4"`.
+- [ ] Same endpoint returns `watermarkFullName` matching the account's display name.
+- [ ] A free preview while signed out returns `watermarkFullName: "مهمان"`.
+- [ ] `POST /lessons/{id}/playback` returns `videoType` and a `type` on each quality.
+- [ ] The shipped web PWA still plays (it ignores every new key).
